.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-LIST-NAMESPACES 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-list-namespaces \- list namespaces under an account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam list-namespaces
.BR \-\-account | \-a
.I ACCOUNTID
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIPREFIX\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-size\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-page\-index\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-sort\-column\fR \fICOLUMN\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the namespaces under an account via the eam service's
.I list-namespaces
action.
.PP
The caller must be a global administrator, or hold account-scoped
administrator privileges on \fIACCOUNTID\fR (see
.BR euclid-cli-eam-grant-namespace-access (1)).
.PP
The JSON response, containing the matching namespaces and the total
namespace count for the account, is printed to standard output.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-account " " \fIACCOUNTID\fR
Only return namespaces belonging to this account. Required.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-prefix " " \fIPREFIX\fR
Only return namespaces whose name starts with \fIPREFIX\fR. If omitted,
all namespaces under the account match.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-page\-size " " \fIN\fR
Maximum number of namespaces to return. \fI0\fR or less (the default,
\fI\-1\fR) means no limit.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-page\-index " " \fIN\fR
Zero-based page index, applied when \fB\-\-page\-size\fR is set. Defaults to
\fI\-1\fR (meaningless while paging is off).
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-sort\-column " " \fICOLUMN\fR
Field to sort by: \fIname\fR (default) or \fIdescription\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing was retrieved.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, the request could not be sent, or the caller lacks
administrator privileges on the account. If the failure was an expired or
invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored credentials file is removed;
run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-namespaces \e
    --account 123456789012
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-namespace (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-namespace (1)
